{"absent":["Locking, concurrency and sleep context rules for pin control handles and mapping tables.","PE parsing, validation, loading and entry invocation logic.","Symbol table, relocation application and data directory consumption semantics.","Enabled pin control core behavior beyond fallback shims.","Personality mask value and permitted personality values.","Header include guard and page constant definitions beyond their names."],"dossier":"D17","findings":[{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_1BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_8192BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_RESERVED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_MASK","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_LNK_NRELOC_OVFL","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_DISCARDABLE","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_NOT_CACHED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_NOT_PAGED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_SHARED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_EXECUTE","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_READ","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_WRITE"],"text":"Section characteristic word reserves bits 20-23 for alignment with mask 0x00f00000; encodings step from 0x00100000 for one byte through 0x00e00000 for 8192 bytes, with 0x00f00000 reserved. High single-bit attributes are overflow 0x01000000, discardable 0x02000000, not cached 0x04000000, not paged 0x08000000, shared 0x10000000, execute 0x20000000, read 0x40000000 and write 0x80000000."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_UNKNOWN","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_COFF","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_CODEVIEW","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_FPO","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_MISC","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_EXCEPTION","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_FIXUP","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_OMAP_TO_SRC","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_OMAP_FROM_SRC","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_BORLAND","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_RESERVED10","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_CLSID","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_VC_FEATURE","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_POGO","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_ILTCG","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_MPX","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_REPRO","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_EMBEDDED_PORTABLE_PDB","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_SPGO","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_PDBCHECKSUM","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_EX_DLLCHARACTERISTICS","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_PERFMAP"],"text":"Debug directory type identifiers run from 0 unknown through 21 PerfMap, covering COFF 1, CodeView 2, FPO 3, misc 4, exception 5, fixup 6, OMAP to source 7, OMAP from source 8, Borland 9, reserved10 10, CLSID 11, VC feature 12, POGO 13, ILTCG 14, MPX 15, repro 16, embedded portable PDB 17, SPGO 18, PDB checksum 19 and extended DLL characteristics 20."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::WIN_CERT_TYPE_PKCS_SIGNED_DATA","include/linux/pe.h::WIN_CERT_TYPE_EFI_OKCS115","include/linux/pe.h::WIN_CERT_TYPE_EFI_GUID","include/linux/pe.h::WIN_CERT_REVISION_1_0","include/linux/pe.h::WIN_CERT_REVISION_2_0"],"text":"Certificate catalog uses type 0x0002 for PKCS signed data, 0x0EF0 for EFI OKCS115 and 0x0EF1 for EFI GUID, with revision 0x0100 for 1.0 and 0x0200 for 2.0."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::x64_coff_reloc_type","include/linux/pe.h::arm_coff_reloc_type","include/linux/pe.h::sh_coff_reloc_type","include/linux/pe.h::ppc_coff_reloc_type","include/linux/pe.h::x86_coff_reloc_type","include/linux/pe.h::ia64_coff_reloc_type"],"text":"Per architecture relocation vocabularies start at zero for absolute and increase by one in declaration order; x64 holds 17 values through SSPAN32, ARM 7 through SECREL, SH 26 through NOMODE, PPC 18 through TOKEN, x86 11 through REL32 and IA64 29 through ADDEND."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::mz_hdr"],"text":"DOS stub header holds mostly 16 bit words for last block size, file pages, relocation count, header paragraphs, extra paragraphs, stack and instruction locations, checksum, relocation table offset, overlay number, reserved gaps and OEM fields, then a 32 bit PE header offset followed by variable length message bytes."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::mz_reloc"],"text":"DOS relocation entry pairs a 16 bit offset with a 16 bit segment value."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::pe_hdr"],"text":"COFF file header starts with 32 bit signature, then machine and section counts, timestamp, symbol table location and count, optional header length and flag word using 16 and 32 bit fields."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::pe32_opt_hdr","include/linux/pe.h::pe32plus_opt_hdr"],"text":"32 bit optional header carries linker versions, text data and bss sizes, entry offset, code and data bases, then load address, alignments, OS image and subsystem versions, runtime version, image and header sizes, checksum, subsystem and DLL flags, stack and heap reservations, loader flags and directory count. 64 bit variant omits data base, widens load address and stack and heap reservations to 64 bits and otherwise preserves the same logical sequence."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::data_dirent","include/linux/pe.h::data_directory"],"text":"Data directory is a fixed sequence of 16 address plus size pairs ordered exports, imports, resources, exceptions, certificates, base relocations, debug, architecture, global pointer, TLS, load config, bound imports, import addresses, delay imports, CLR runtime header and reserved, each pair holding an address relative to load base and a byte size."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::section_header"],"text":"Section table entry holds an eight byte name that may encode a string table offset, loaded size, relative virtual address, raw size, file pointers to data, relocations and line numbers, 16 bit relocation and line counts and a 32 bit characteristic flag word."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::coff_reloc","include/linux/pe.h::coff_reloc.anon_1"],"text":"COFF relocation record holds virtual address and symbol index as 32 bit words plus a 16 bit type selector shared as architecture specific enumeration or raw value covering x64 ARM SH PPC x86 and IA64 vocabularies."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::win_certificate"],"text":"Certificate header is eight bytes with 32 bit total length and two 16 bit revision and type selectors."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::win_certificate","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_map_type","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_map_mux","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_map_configs","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_map","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_map.anon_1"],"text":"Pin control mapping record identifies consumer device, desired state name, mapping kind and controller device, with payload either mux group plus function names or target pin or group name plus configuration array length and pointer. Kind enumeration orders invalid, dummy state, mux group, per pin configs and per group configs."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/pfn.h::PFN_ALIGN","include/linux/pfn.h::PFN_PHYS","include/linux/pfn.h::PHYS_PFN"],"text":"Frame helpers round an address up to page boundary, convert a frame number to a byte address by left shift and convert a byte address to a frame number by right shift using page size, mask and shift parameters."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/personality.h::personality","include/linux/personality.h::set_personality"],"text":"Personality accessor isolates selected bits through a mask constant while the setter stores the supplied value into the current task field."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_DUMMY_STATE","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_MUX_GROUP","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_MUX_GROUP_DEFAULT","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_MUX_GROUP_HOG","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_MUX_GROUP_HOG_DEFAULT","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_PIN","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_PIN_DEFAULT","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_PIN_HOG","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_PIN_HOG_DEFAULT","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_GROUP","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_GROUP_DEFAULT","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_GROUP_HOG","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::PIN_MAP_CONFIGS_GROUP_HOG_DEFAULT"],"text":"Mapping constructor helpers build static table entries for dummy states, mux selections and pin or group configurations, with shorthand forms supplying default state name, self hosted controller name or array length automatically."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_get","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_put","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_lookup_state","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_select_state","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::devm_pinctrl_get","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::devm_pinctrl_put","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_select_default_state","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_default_state.alt_1","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_init_state.alt_1","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state.alt_1","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_idle_state.alt_1","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_default_state.alt_2","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_init_state.alt_2","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state.alt_2","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_pm_select_idle_state.alt_2"],"text":"When pin control support is unavailable the consumer interface degrades to trivial results: handle acquisition and state lookup yield null, selection and power state helpers report success and release operations do nothing."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_gpio_can_use_line","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_gpio_request","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_gpio_free","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_gpio_direction_input","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_gpio_direction_output","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_gpio_get_config","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_gpio_set_config"],"text":"GPIO integration shims report the line as usable, accept requests, direction changes and configuration updates with success and ignore release."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_register_mappings","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::devm_pinctrl_register_mappings","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_unregister_mappings","include/linux/pinctrl/machine.h::pinctrl_provide_dummies"],"text":"Board mapping registration helpers succeed without recording anything, while unregistration and dummy provisioning are empty operations."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_get_select","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_get_select_default","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::devm_pinctrl_get_select","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::devm_pinctrl_get_select_default"],"text":"Combined acquisition helpers expose an acquire plus activate contract keyed by state name with default state shorthand and managed and unmanaged ownership flavors; success transfers an owned handle to the caller while lookup or activation failure releases partial state and propagates an error indicator."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/pe.h::mz_hdr","include/linux/pe.h::section_header","include/linux/pe.h::pe32_opt_hdr","include/linux/pe.h::pe_hdr","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_get","include/linux/pinctrl/consumer.h::pinctrl_select_state"],"text":"Parsers must bound the trailing DOS message against file length, treat eight byte section names as possibly unterminated or indirection encoded, and validate directory, section and relocation counts before indexing tables; fallback pin control shims returning null or success can mask missing hardware support if callers do not distinguish disabled builds."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":105,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"927ee632d14b551f83fe7a9f162d15595fedc350d6bff7bdce52995e491e86d4","prompt_sha256":"3fdabc3f44108ed179fc6329abfe8ddfa520227f170d4563a31eb685f715bff0","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_1BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_2BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_4BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_8BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_16BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_32BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_64BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_128BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_256BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_512BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_1024BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_2048BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_4096BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_8192BYTES","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_RESERVED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_ALIGN_MASK","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_LNK_NRELOC_OVFL","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_DISCARDABLE","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_NOT_CACHED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_NOT_PAGED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_SHARED","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_EXECUTE","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_READ","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_SCN_MEM_WRITE","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_UNKNOWN","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_COFF","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_CODEVIEW","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_FPO","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_MISC","include/linux/pe.h::IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_EXCEPTION","include/linux